    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1076">

                <pb facs="1331" n="1317" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/2–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-16T19:00:00-04:00">February 16,
                            1945—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. It is agreed by the State, War, and Navy Departments that Military and Naval
                    Staff conversations with Peru should start March 19. Refer Department’s secret
                    circular instruction August 1, 1944,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d1076-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="1332" n="1318" xml:id="pg1318"/> January 10, 1945.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d1076-f2"/> Please consult the Foreign Minister and cable Department
                    whether that date is agreeable to the Peruvian Government.</p>
                <p>Conversations in Peru will be under the supervision of General Brett<anchor
                        n="25" xml:id="d1076-f3"/> and Admiral Kingman.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d1076-f4"/> They will get in touch with you directly concerning
                    details of the conversations. General Brett will provide you with a program
                    outlining the purpose of the conversations and the topics to be discussed. On
                    receipt of it please transmit the program to the Peruvian authorities, unless
                    you receive [<hi rendition="#italic">perceive</hi>] objection in order that they
                    may be prepared in advance.</p>
                <p>It is emphasized that the forthcoming staff conversations are entirely
                    exploratory in nature, will involve no commitments by either party, and will be
                    confined to technical military and naval discussions, not to include political
                        matters.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d1076-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
