            <note corresp="#d1076-f2" n="24" xml:id="d1076-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg600">p. 600</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1076-f3" n="25" xml:id="d1076-f3-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. George H. Brett, Commanding General, Caribbean Defense Command.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1076-f4" n="26" xml:id="d1076-f4-content">
                <p>Rear Adm. Howard F. Kingman, Commander, Panama Sea Frontier.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1076-f5" n="27" xml:id="d1076-f5-content">
                <p>Ambassador White reported in his telegram 181, February 23, 1945, midnight, that
                    Peru was agreeable to the beginning of conversations (810.20
                    Defense/2–2345).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
